layoff series / 104 team-offense units; compare rank orderings own-PPP vs net-swing.\n- observed_verdict: descriptive\n- observed_failure_type: E_unclear\n- observed_notes: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_confidence: medium (0.65)\n- auto_addresses_question: RQC:RQC-006"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-032", "score": 0.101, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-032 | Study family SF-APPA-032: Execution conformance scoring ORL vs DET\n- observed_research_question: Execution conformance scoring ORL vs DET\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: Measure how closely each team executed the recommended opener.\n- observed_result: ORL avg leverage |d| 12.6pp, scores 86.3/87.4; DET 7.7pp, 82.3/92.3; DET matched opener #3.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY\n- observed_failure_evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_sample_and_power: 1 game\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPS-017\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF32\n- observed_method: One game, 2 offenses; leverage-weighted conformance scores.\n- observed_verdict: descriptive\n- observed_failure_type: E_unclear\n- observed_notes: DET note says it 'nailed the high-leverage moves' while PULL_UP was +10.2pp over the recommendation.\n- auto_confidence: medium (0.65)"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-085", "score": 0.094, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-085 | Study family SF-APPS-085: Connector teammate-path quality Q_p split-half reliability\n- observed_research_question: Connector teammate-path quality Q_p split-half reliability\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: Connector quality Q_p (teammate-initiated on-off PPP gap) is a stable player-season attribute.\n- observed_result: Pearson r(Q_a,Q_b)=+0.215 p=0.0297; Spearman rho=+0.242. Spearman-Brown Q~0.355, S~0.278. Sign agreement 65.7% (67/102) binomial p=0.000996. ICC(player-season)=0.216 (78.4% within). Attenuation: even a perfect predictor  [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:low_measurement_reliability\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MEASURE_RELIABILITY\n- observed_failure_evidence: Split-half r=0.215 / SB 0.355 is too low to treat Q_p as a stable scoutable trait; most variance is within-player half-to-half.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=102 connectors\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPS-086"}], "n_results": 4}

