  "historical_effect": {
    "changed_decision": "yes",
    "explanation": "The retrieval of APPS-085 demonstrates that a naive split-half reliability test on a derived performance metric can return untestable results due to low measurement reliability. Combined with APPA-005 showing that inferential labels for defensive adjustments are noisy, these findings motivated a design that avoids assumed labels, incorporates extensive controls for game context, and uses a hierarchical model to jointly estimate reliability, rather than relying on a simple raw correlation."
