    {
      "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
      "text": "With 120 team-seasons, the study has limited power to detect a small between-team ICC; if the true ICC is < 0.1, the estimate will be too imprecise to conclude reliability."
    },
    {
      "code": "DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY",
      "text": "Defensive schemes and personnel change across seasons; reliability measured within a season may not hold across seasons, and using multiple seasons may introduce drift."
    },
    {
      "code": "RTM_SELECTION",
      "text": "If teams are selected based on extreme raw values in one period, regression to the mean may inflate the apparent reliability in a subsequent period if not properly handled by hierarchical shrinkage."
